  "description": "meme-id: trump_be_thinking; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts Donald Trump with a smug expression and includes text suggesting he is thinking, 'you can't lose in 2020 if there is no 2020.' This is a satirical take on his political strategy and perceived lack of concern for the consequences of a non-existent election. The intent is to mock his approach to politics and his potential disregard for democratic norms or the legitimacy of the electoral process. While not explicitly abusive or hateful toward a protected group, the meme is harmful as it promotes a cynical view of political leadership and could be interpreted as endorsing or normalizing the idea of undermining democratic institutions. The humor is derived from the absurdity of the situation, but it risks normalizing political manipulation and could be seen as propagandistic in its implication that political figures might prioritize personal gain over democratic integrity.",
